# Frappe JavaScript Patterns

## Client Scripts

Frappe uses global variables like `frappe`, `cur_frm`, `__()` for translations.

```javascript
// ✅ Form script pattern
frappe.ui.form.on("My DocType", {
    refresh(frm) {
        frm.set_query("item_code", () => ({
            filters: { is_stock_item: 1 }
        }));
    },

    validate(frm) {
        if (!frm.doc.qty) {
            frappe.throw(__("Quantity is required"));
        }
    }
});
```

## API Calls

```javascript
// ✅ Preferred - frappe.call
frappe.call({
    method: "production_entry_app.api.get_data",
    args: { work_order: frm.doc.name },
    callback: (r) => {
        if (r.message) {
            frm.set_value("data", r.message);
        }
    }
});
```

## Translations

Always wrap user-facing strings with `__()`:

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
frappe.msgprint("Operation completed");

// ✅ GOOD
frappe.msgprint(__("Operation completed"));
```

## Avoid console.log

ESLint is configured to warn on `console.log`. Remove before committing.
